Now begin by inspecting the existing StatusPop repository.

Do not immediately implement all the proposed features.

First establish the actual state of the codebase, identify what already works, run the available baseline checks, and produce a prioritized implementation plan.

Then implement only the next approved phase.

If I later say "continue", proceed to the next phase only after verifying that the previous phase is stable. If a blocker requires a decision from me, stop and ask a focused question.

**Final instruction:** Build a coherent, maintainable product that grows from the existing StatusPop application. Every change must preserve working functionality, have a clear economic purpose for small vendors, and be testable before the next change begins.